ks and piece coordination. Other options like pawn advances or bishop moves are less immediately impactful.\n\nReason: The queen move maximizes piece activity and central control, which is critical in the opening. It also avoids moving pawns unnecessarily and keeps the queen safe from immediate threats.\n\nAnswer: Q: d1-d2'}
